# Pinned upstream sources for the mihomo core and its QNX dependency overrides.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# The BB10/QNX build of mihomo needs 7 dependency modules patched for QNX (the OS
# is not in Go's standard build-tag set, so each module needs a *_qnx.go port and
# a one-line build-tag tweak on the generic unix file it would otherwise match).
# Historically those patches lived as absolute-path `replace` forks in sibling
# directories, which is not reproducible. This file + patches/ + apply-patches.sh
# make the override tree regenerable from pinned upstream + small committed diffs.
#
# Format:
#   mihomo  <import-path>  <git-commit>  <local-dir>
#     -> scripts/fetch-mihomo.sh blobless-clones the mihomo core at that commit into
#        mihomo/<local-dir>/ and applies patches/mihomo.patch (the QNX DNS port).
#   module  <import-path>  <version>  <local-name>
#     -> scripts/apply-patches.sh fetches <import-path>@<version>, copies it to
#        mihomo/overrides-upstream/<local-name>, then applies patches/<local-name>.patch.
#        <local-name> is also the basename of the patch file.

# mihomo core (main module). Base commit identified by matching go.mod's require set
# + the Nov-11 file timestamps to metacubex/mihomo's Alpha branch; the local delta is
# a 5-file QNX patch (dns packetconn split + go.mod go-directive bump / yaml.v3 /
# x/sys replace). Verified: a pristine checkout + patches/mihomo.patch reproduces the
# source byte-identical, and the QNX binary built from it is identical to the legacy
# sibling-tree build (modulo the embedded override path; see REFACTOR-PLAN.md).
